A||||1||kempton||erratic idle with new TPS
Z||000000||kempton||08-17-99||06:42 PM||||  My 86 SE 4-speed manual has an erratic idle. I replaced the TPS as well as rebuilding the top end of the engine with new lifters. When I disconnect the IAC below the TPS, the erratic idle stop, and it no longer stalls, but it idles over 2000 rpms, way too high. When I plug the IAC back in, it idles erratically. Could this be a bunk TPS? How can I tell if the IAC needs replacing. Also, the shop that did the rebuild wanted to replace the pistons, rods, rings and bearings. They were saying that 2 of the cylinders are weak. But it should run better, not worse. But all I went in there for was a new head gasket, which I replaced along with the plenum gasket and lifters. Now the engine kicks around a lot. Also, when I shift into 1st, sometimes I think it's in 1st and when I go to accelerate, it pops out of gear. Only happens on 1st gear. Anyone got any ideas?
Z||000001||mwbackus||08-18-99||06:30 PM||||Pull the IAC and clean it.  If that does not fix the problem, replace it.  It sounds like you have a real problem with your transmission mounts, together with some very constrictive routing of your shift cables.  IE..the drivetrain movement is sufficient to pull on the shift cable, causing it to jump out of gear.<p>Mike
